  "predicted_delta_text": "**Prediction**: s11_db improves by ~3.5 dB.  \n*Reasoning*: The input node (n1) is connected directly to L1 and C1, forming a resonant input structure. However, the gate of NM1 (n2) is biased via R1-R2, making the input impedance sensitive to bias point and parasitics. Introducing PM3 (PMOS) with drain tied to n1 (input), gate to n2, source to VDD, creates a feedback path from output to input via the gate. This is a **source-degenerated PMOS feedback** that actively stabilizes the input impedance. The PM3 acts as a voltage-controlled current source pulling current from the input node, effectively increasing the input resistance and enabling better matching to 50\u03a9. The structure is similar to a common-gate amplifier with feedback, enhancing input match at the cost of some gain \u2014 but the binding metric s11_db is improved significantly due to better impedance scaling.\n\n---",
